{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And they placed incense upon it.</b> Meaning, upon the fire — for nowhere do we find incense being offered upon the pan." "<b>A foreign fire, which He had not commanded them.</b> That is, He had already warned them not to do so, as it is written ״ולא תעלו אש זרה״, and also He did not command them — meaning He did not permit it to them for the time being, for sometimes the Holy One, blessed be He, forbids a thing and permits it for the time being, to magnify His name among the nations, as we find with Elijah on Mount Carmel, who offered on a bamah by divine word during the period when bamos were forbidden. And likewise we may explain ״לשרוף את בניה באש אשר לא צויתי״ etc."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:55.428146737Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}